CVSign 1/3: pass TLP's lift-pooling regularisers through to the loss

Why: CVSign adopts "the Temporal Decoder from TLP" (Sec. III, Implementation
Details). The Dockerfile replaces CorrNet's modules/tconv.py with TLP's pinned
tconv.py, whose Temporal_LiftPool returns the predictor/updater regularisers
loss_LiftPool_u/p. CorrNet's SLRModel drops them; this forwards them and adds
the Cu/Cp loss terms exactly as TLP's slr_network.py criterion_calculation
does (weights set in configs/cvsign.yaml, from TLP's configs/baseline.yaml).
Applies to: CorrNet @ 5a361cc709ae8f697f4c9e23760e64c2daa8f744 after TLP tconv.py copy
---
diff --git a/slr_network.py b/slr_network.py
index 9d49a0d..6d71a8d 100644
--- a/slr_network.py
+++ b/slr_network.py
@@ -109,6 +109,8 @@ class SLRModel(nn.Module):
             "sequence_logits": outputs,
             "conv_sents": conv_pred,
             "recognized_sents": pred,
+            "loss_LiftPool_u": conv1d_outputs['loss_LiftPool_u'],
+            "loss_LiftPool_p": conv1d_outputs['loss_LiftPool_p'],
         }
 
     def criterion_calculation(self, ret_dict, label, label_lgt):
@@ -126,6 +128,10 @@ class SLRModel(nn.Module):
                 loss += weight * self.loss['distillation'](ret_dict["conv_logits"],
                                                            ret_dict["sequence_logits"].detach(),
                                                            use_blank=False)
+            elif k == 'Cu':
+                loss += weight * ret_dict["loss_LiftPool_u"]
+            elif k == 'Cp':
+                loss += weight * ret_dict["loss_LiftPool_p"]
         return loss
 
     def criterion_init(self):
